# Everything here is OPTIONAL. Boxes runs with no .env at all:
#
#   docker compose up -d        ->  http://localhost:3000
#
# Copy this file to .env only to change something. Whatever it contains
# reaches the orchestrator as-is; compose.yaml names nothing in it but the two
# credentials below. The values shown commented out are the defaults, and they
# live in orchestrator/src/config.ts, which parses and validates all of this
# at boot.

# ---- where the port is published ----
# Loopback by default, because the orchestrator has no authentication of its
# own. Change this only when something else is providing that auth: a reverse
# proxy on this host already reaches 127.0.0.1, and one in a container should
# join the `boxes_default` network and use `orchestrator:3000` instead.
#BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
#HOST_PORT=3000

# ---- credentials ----
# Without a Claude token, sessions start and the gateway works, but no agent
# turn can run. `claude setup-token` prints one, tied to a subscription rather
# than to an API key.
#
# Anything with access to the working directory can read this file. To keep a
# credential out of every file, export it instead — compose passes these two
# names through from the shell, and an exported value wins over this file:
#
#   export PROFILE_DEFAULT_CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...
#   docker compose up -d
#
# That pass-through is why these two names, alone among the settings here,
# cannot come from an env file outside the repo: BOXES_ENV feeds env_file,
# and compose lets the pass-through override it even when the shell is empty.
# Put a credential in the shell or in ./.env; BOXES_ENV still carries the rest.
# A credential set here never reaches a session container. The egress proxy
# holds it and swaps it onto the wire; the session gets a worthless
# placeholder of the same shape. See README, "What a session can reach".
#PROFILE_DEFAULT_CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...
#PROFILE_DEFAULT_GH_TOKEN=ghp_...            # classic PAT for the bot account
#PROFILE_DEFAULT_GIT_NAME=boxes-bot
#PROFILE_DEFAULT_GIT_EMAIL=boxes-bot@users.noreply.github.com

# ---- egress ----
# Hosts sessions may reach, comma or whitespace separated. Exact names and
# one-label wildcards (`*.example.com` matches `a.example.com`, not
# `a.b.example.com` and not `example.com`). Unset is the default: any public
# host, with private ranges still denied.
#
# The hosts of a credential you configured above are always reachable, so a
# narrow list can never cut a session off from inference or from GitHub.
#EGRESS_ALLOWED_HOSTS=github.com,*.github.com,*.githubusercontent.com,api.anthropic.com,registry.npmjs.org

# ---- gateway ----
# Left unset, the orchestrator generates a token on first boot and keeps it in
# the data volume, so it survives restarts. Set one here to pin or rotate it.
#WS_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ---- sessions ----
#SESSION_IMAGE=boxes-session:latest
#SESSION_SUBNET_POOL=10.200.0.0/16
#SESSION_MEM_LIMIT=4g
#SESSION_CPUS=2
#SESSION_PIDS_LIMIT=512
#IDLE_STOP_MINUTES=30

# ---- permissions ----
# hold | deny -- what to do with a permission request nobody answered in time.
#PERMISSION_FALLBACK=hold
#PERMISSION_HOLD_MINUTES=120
#NTFY_URL=                                   # POSTed when a session wants you

# ---- notifications ----
# Web Push needs no configuration: the deployment generates a VAPID keypair
# into DATA_DIR the first time a browser subscribes. This is only the contact
# a push service uses when it has a problem with what we send it; a mailto: or
# an https: URL, and nothing else.
#PUSH_SUBJECT=https://github.com/splitbrain/boxes
